# Cross-platform product parity

Source Bridge is **one shared product**. Desktop web, mobile web, Android PWA, iPhone/iPad PWA, and desktop PWA must share the same product behaviour, APIs, auth, messaging, payments, Live, and Opportunities — **no platform forks**.

## Requirements

- Implement features once in the shared Next.js app; do not create separate mobile-only or PWA-only business logic forks.
- Consider **installed / standalone** mode (safe areas, back behaviour, no trapped external links, no force-refresh during forms).
- Service worker: keep `/api/`, auth, payments, messaging, Live, and private personalized routes **network-only**. No offline mutation replay queues.
- iPhone Manual QA may remain pending, but implementation must not ignore iOS installed-mode constraints.
- Final delivery reports for user-facing work must include **cross-platform coverage** with PASS / FAIL / PENDING per surface (desktop web, mobile web, Android PWA, iOS PWA, desktop PWA).

## Non-goals

- This rule does **not** weaken the payment production freeze (`00-payment-production-freeze.mdc`).
- This rule does not require shipping native App Store / Play Store packages.
